WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.469
I'm a huge fan of John Mulaney's,

00:00:01.469 --> 00:00:03.290
as I think we all are,

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.730
but you do a great John
Mulaney impression.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.160
I think for him, I was just kind of...

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.780
I think I watched his
stand ups, a few specials,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.757
and I was thinking of
like, he always goes,

00:00:14.757 --> 00:00:17.670
"I've noticed, when I wear my pants,

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.780
sometimes I do have ants in
my pants, and that's a saying,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.810
but it's true to my life."

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.530
It's always saying like
I notice something.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.108
An observation.

00:00:28.108 --> 00:00:30.000
(Conan and Melissa laughing)

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.520
And then, yeah.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.950
He's got kind of an old
fashioned sort of diction,

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.900
and I mean he could be in Vaudeville.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.507
It could be 1922 when here's
John Mulaney, you know.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:44.008
Yeah, you saw it on the SNL at home.

00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:46.630
He was in the Masterclass sketch,

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.800
where he's a master at putting on suits,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.110
putting together your tie and your button,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.170
look like you're going to
your First Holy Communion.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.717
And he saw it and he really liked it.

00:00:57.717 --> 00:01:00.410
And I noticed he does a certain
thing when's he's walking.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.243
He goes...

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:04.419
You know?

00:01:04.419 --> 00:01:05.252
(Conan laughing)

00:01:05.252 --> 00:01:08.330
You know what, one of the
impressions that you do,

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.070
I'm just talking about how
you'll pick an unusual target,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.800
The Little Rascals.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.350
The Little Rascals is something
that I grew up watching

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.810
and it's from the 1930's,
but they would show it a lot

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.290
on local television when I was a kid.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.110
That's how I know it.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.850
I didn't even know that someone your age

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.030
would be aware of The Little Rascals.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.700
We would rent The Little
Rascals VHS, the classics.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.580
Oh good, okay.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:33.220
But the past few months, my mom,

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.900
she let me borrow her Little Rascal DVDs,

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.808
and she said, "give 'em back
'cause these are my favorite."

00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:39.960
(woman laughing)

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.480
I'm not gonna keep 'em.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.313
No.

00:01:42.313 --> 00:01:43.420
Yeah but-

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.990
And so you learned, you
started watching those

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.200
and I'm told you do a
Little Rascals impression

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.367
or an impression of The Little Rascals.

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:52.380
Well 'cause I was trying
to watch Little Rascals

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.960
and I couldn't even
get through an episode.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.570
I don't know what they're saying.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:59.240
You can't hear it it's so
crinkly and old, you know?

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.690
They're just like (mumbling).

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.246
Hamburger.

00:02:09.246 --> 00:02:13.170
(Conan and Melissa laughing)

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.480
That's all I could hear so.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.750
Yeah, that's pretty much all it is.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.860
And also long takes.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.120
They'll do like...

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.060
They'll be visuals of like Spanky looking

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.740
or Alfalfa looking at
something or somebody,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.573
Buckwheat, I don't know,

00:02:24.573 --> 00:02:26.980
they'll just be looking at
something and they'll be like...

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.980
And the camera will be
on them way too long

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.513
and you think they just had
more time in the 1930's.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.173
You know, comedy now is
like (snapping fingers)

00:02:38.173 --> 00:02:40.340
it's like this and back then,

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.520
someone would do something funny

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.470
and they'd cut to someone else going...

00:02:44.513 --> 00:02:48.120
(Melissa laughing)

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.038
Yeah.

00:02:49.038 --> 00:02:49.871
And you're like, what?

00:02:49.871 --> 00:02:52.024
You just had more time
during the Depression.

00:02:52.024 --> 00:02:54.573
Was the film expensive then?

